 "interpretation": [
  "The stored results are read only after their SHA-256 has been compared with 'figures_v2.source_sha256' of the conditions. The run script, the library files and the versions of numpy and scipy must equal those recorded in the stored results. The tiles use the grid 'figures_v2.grid_N' (checked against the first grid of the results), and every readout stored for that grid is compared with the regenerated one to within 1e-12 (booleans exactly) before any figure is drawn. These readouts do not fix the image pixel by pixel; the identity of the images rests on the identity of the code and the inputs.",
  "Panel (a) shows the window [-w, w]^2 of the (V, A) plane, w from the conditions; the script stops before drawing if a shown point of any figure lies outside its window. An inset shows the whole square [-1, 1]^2 with the window as a rectangle; the centre (0, 0) is marked with a cross in both.",
  "Labels: coincident points of one text share one label ('(no term)' only when all of them are unmatched; a mix stops the script). After the layout is drawn, each label is placed 7 pt from its point in the first of eight directions (ordered by their angle to the direction away from the mean of the distinct shown points) in which it stays inside panel (a) and overlaps no earlier label, the legend, the inset, a point or the centre cross (3 pt around each). The layout is drawn again and every condition is checked on the final boxes; the script stops if one fails.",
  "All figures are drawn into a temporary directory; they and the JSON are moved into results/ only after every figure has been drawn. The script refuses to start if any of its outputs exists."
 ],
